\n\nThe formula for the differential comes from the multivariable chain rule, which can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the differential can be extended to any number of variables. For example, for a three-variable function $f(x,y,z),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125813 #edb/ref 1065 4191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125813 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "549aa462-1d86-5880-b6e2-2f6b1d79b41d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125813 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125814 #edb/ref 1064 "Given a multivariable function $f(x,y),$ the differential\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ntells us how infinitesimal changes in $x$ and $y,$ denoted $\\textrm dx$ and $\\textrm dy,$ result in an infinitesimal change in $f,$ denoted $\\textrm df.$\n\nConsequently, we can use the differential to *approximate* the change in $f$ as we move from one point to another. If we move from a point $(x,y)$ to a point $(x + \\Delta x, y + \\Delta y),$ then the approximate change in $f$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf(x,y) & ≈(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,Δx+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,Δy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above formula is very similar to the differential formula, except the $\\textrm d$'s are replaced with $\\Delta$'s. The $\\textrm d$'s refer to infinitesimal changes, while the $\\Delta$'s refer to changes that can actually be measured." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125814 #edb/ref 1065 4214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125814 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c2d5565a-cb57-537b-bd6e-64ebd0b91783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125814 #edb/ref 1067 "Approximating Change Using Differentials" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282101 #edb/ref 1080 "-0.521" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282101 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282101 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e9f4654-e89d-5d9e-a79c-0bb5f857defd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282842 #edb/ref 1080 "-0.652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282842 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186282842 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "85c51f51-7216-584b-b827-69d84ec4f79d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283346 #edb/ref 1080 "-0.359" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283346 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283346 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "beb360a4-ee13-5f31-9c0a-e76bcd78e6b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283667 #edb/ref 1080 "-0.482" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283667 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283667 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e2d331ae-1ad5-5557-89ef-e15bbaae3a68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283703 #edb/ref 1080 "-0.274" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283703 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186283703 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e74c9b4d-a866-5c53-8a6c-93a7e66b72ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186283346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284241 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aff6cf4f-69f4-50e0-b11a-e6431b91e83f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284581 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284581 #edb/ref 1069 "q-167171" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284581 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284581 #edb/ref 1071 "Estimate $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)$ at the point $({\\pi }^{2},0).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284581 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9eb149a3-bdcc-552e-a682-ced670cd4013" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284581 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{x}+y)\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $({\\pi }^{2},0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x-\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $({\\pi }^{2}+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,Δx-\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2)=f({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $({\\pi }^{2},0)$ to $({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =({\\pi }^{2}+1)-{\\pi }^{2}=1, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈(-\\frac{1}{2\\pi })\\cdot (1)-1\\cdot (0.2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }-0.2 \\\\  & ≈-0.359.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ decreases by about $-0.359.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({\\pi }^{2}+1,0.2) & ≈f({\\pi }^{2},0)-0.359 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}+0.2) & ≈\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}+0)-0.359 \\\\  & =0-0.359 \\\\  & =-0.359.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345359 #edb/ref 1080 "40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345359 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345359 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "009c9900-f889-52f9-b00b-40100c9397c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345374 #edb/ref 1080 "(2x+3{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345374 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345374 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02dad359-25f2-59b1-a326-992f7d8f2be8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345456 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345456 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345456 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d5f0ff3-67c3-5156-80d4-3b1056e54271" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345569 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345569 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345569 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "18aa2d29-4200-55a9-9049-eec28d6ce46d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345717 #edb/ref 1080 "1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345717 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345717 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28d8915f-3339-5227-a3ee-86c79928eb21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345803 #edb/ref 1080 "17\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345803 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345803 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "33de2cd4-781a-5e11-9d06-401da624c0ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345828 #edb/ref 1080 "(2x+3{x}^{2}y)\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}-3{y}^{2})\\text{d}y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345828 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345828 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37a0854b-5ffd-53b5-a97e-3fc8c049dafa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345843 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17